# v1.20b FLEET RETRAIN — the same eight, against a tree that charts correctly.
#
# This supersedes scripts/campaigns/v1_20_fleet.jobs, which was stopped after
# four members because the tree it was training against was defective.
#
# WHAT WENT WRONG. #42 added a guarded `parent.subordinate_ids.append(successor.id)`
# to core/units.py::_fill_vacancy and thereby made the pre-existing
# `successor.subordinate_ids.append(promoted.id)` redundant — but that older line
# had no `not in` guard, so both fired and the backfilled agent was linked into
# its new leader TWICE. It triggers on the commonest succession in the game: kill
# SL1 in `squad` and TL1's chart reads ['TL2', 'RFN1', 'RFN1']. Since
# living_subordinates is what observations.py writes into the four subordinate
# slots and what actions.py indexes with order_slot, the promoted root observed a
# phantom subordinate and carried two distinct ORDER indices addressing one agent
# — inside the very fix meant to make the promoted branch observable and
# orderable. Fixed in da24b42; found by the #49 investigation.
#
# The four members trained against the defective tree — fireteam_v10,
# fireteam_defend_v21, squad_v16, squad_recon_v9, plus a killed partial
# squad_screen_v12 — are KEPT, not deleted. They are the evidence behind
# squad_v16's mute-commander finding and they are the only corpus measuring what
# the double-link cost. None of them may become a baseline member.
#
# Same scenarios, same step budgets, same seed 12 as the v1.19 members, so the
# only thing differing from the shipping fleet is the tree. Sequential in one
# nohup'd queue: ~8 runs x 25-45 min.
#
# THE OPEN QUESTION THIS FLEET ANSWERS. squad_v16 trained to a mute commander —
# 0 root claims in 1,865 admissible root steps, closed_on_root_report_rate 0.000,
# gate FAIL — while its matched v1.19-tree arm squad_v15_bonus1 (same seed, same
# steps, identical prices) filed 196 at 0.866. The double-link CANNOT close the
# DONE channel on its own: is_root_opord_claim and is_done_admissible never read
# subordinates. So squad here is the measurement — if squad_v17 reports normally,
# the defect explains it; if it is mute again, something else is silencing the
# commander and root_done_bonus=1.0 is back under question.
#
# After this lands: publish_baseline.py at N=100, then baseline.py --seal, then
# results_table.py --write. The v1.19 members stay in place until their
# replacements beat them; a MISS supersedes nothing without an ask.
fireteam_v11          --scenario fireteam        --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12
fireteam_defend_v22   --scenario fireteam_defend --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12
squad_v17             --scenario squad           --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
squad_recon_v10       --scenario squad_recon     --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
squad_screen_v13      --scenario squad_screen    --total-steps 2500000 --seed 12
patrol_brique_v7      --scenario patrol_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
defend_brique_v16     --scenario defend_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
platoon_v7            --scenario platoon         --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
